# XCU uucp
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# uucp copies files between systems over a communications line; the page
# defines nothing a script can observe without a configured remote system,
# so the module is recorded as untestable and a transfer is never started by
# the suite.

assertion  XCU.uucp.001
anchor     utilities/uucp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/uucp.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/uucp.html#OPERANDS
class      untestable
since      1992
says       uucp copies the source files to the destination, either of which
           can be system-name!pathname, queueing the job and (with -j)
           writing a job identification to standard output, with -c, -C, -d,
           -f, -m, -n and -r changing how the copy is made.
reason     A transfer needs a configured remote system and a communications
           line that a test system need not have, and a request that does
           succeed leaves a queued job or a file on another machine; the
           diagnostic when no communications means exist is not worded by
           the page.
